# E §11 (tally 2.1.3, issue #58): `REQ-ASK` "in every shape of reality (a plain one, one with scenarios, a joint
# model)". The reality of L4_6_scenario_layer_first: a base and its scenario sc, both loading. The request names qs
# (sc's ask), then zz, an ask of neither world, so the run prints the one refusal and qs isn't answered. Was qs's
# answer alone: refcore skipped the unknown ask silently (T's SR-1, the 34 sets with scenarios).
=== base.tally
model base
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2028-12-31

source s "s"

index ns = 1..10
input x[n in ns]: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  x[3] = 1

ask qb: x[3] law 2027-06-01
=== sc.tally
scenario sc over base
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version w
  cite s
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-06-01
  x[1..5] = 2

ask qs: x[3] in sc law 2027-06-01
=== expect qs zz
refused: REQ-ASK no ask zz
